 trouble.".Here, let me plant these flowers for you."MDo my eyes deceive me?! Did it swap places with different bird Pokémon?"dNo... This is unmistakingly the same Pokémon as before, yet it looks completely different now!"\Sigh, well it looks like it took a liking to these pink flowers too, so that's no good."|You know, I saw a patch of \C[2]Red Flowers\C[0] growing near Mt. Moon. I'm sure that these would be perfect for the garden!"9Hopefully the bird Pokémon won't like them as much."HThat's it! Those are precisely the red flowers I was talking about!"8Here's a another little something for your trouble."CI cannot believe it! It's devouring these red flowers as well!"3And it even changed its appearance once again!"'My, my, what an awkward situation."Hmm..."Oh, I've been such a fool!"�You see, all the flowers that we've planted so far grow nearby, so it's only natural that this Pokémon already has an appetite for them."~If we could find a different type of flower that does not grow around Pewter City, then surely it would leave them alone!"�There are some \C[1]Blue Flowers\C[0] that grow on the other side of Mt. Moon. If you could find me some, then I'm sure that it would solve our problem once and for all!"sI saw a patch of \C[2]Red Flowers\C[0] growing near Mt. Moon. Surely the bird Pokémon will leave those alone."<I would be very grateful if you could pick some for me."IThat's it! Those are precisely the blue flowers I was talking about!"3I'll go ahead and plant these flowers for you."5Misery! It's fond of these blue flowers as well!"!Huh? Won't you look at this!"fIt looks like the bird Pokémon has taken a real liking to you for bringing all of these flowers!"'Oricorio wants to join your party!"8Oricorio forced itself into one of your PokéBalls!"[Well that's certainly one way to solve this problem. I'm quite grateful for your help!"!And so is Oricorio it seems!"9Here's one last reward for helping with all of this."mNow make sure to feed Oricorio plenty of nec