[["kA long time ago, people used to draw life from Pokémon and also give their lives to those Pokémon..."XThat shows that people and Pokémon used to be more closely bonded with each other."�When people moved from place to place, the myths and legends of Pokémon and their power would also be carried with those people."OThat's how myths and legends from each region are blended with each other."{The ancient ruins here have inherited the legends from both the Ruins of Alph in Johto and the Spear Pillar in Sinnoh."UThat is proof that the people from Johto and Sinnoh blended together as a group."I\PN! I did not expect to find you here. It is good to see you again."1My name is Cynthia. I am a Pokémon trainer."=The Sinjoh ruins remind me of Sinnoh, where I come from."EInitially, I thought it was because it snows a lot here as well."But that was not it."=A long time ago... people came from Sinnoh to live here.":They must have built a temple while longing for home."1That's why we call these the Sinjoh ruins..."You are..."A Pokémon trainer?"CThis Pokémon behind you... I can sense a familiar presence...">The power of Dialga... Palkia... Or could it be Giratina?",It's similar, but not quite the same..."Could it be.... Arceus?".Can you come to the Sinjoh ruins with me?"!And bring Arceus with you...["�Il y a bien longtemps, les personnes avaient l'habitude de prendre la vie des Pokémon mais aussi de donner la leur à ces Pokémon en retour..."SCela montre à quel point ces personnes et Pokémon étaient intimement liés."�Quand ces personnes se déplaçaient d'un endroit à un autre, les mythes et légendes des Pokémon ainsi que leur pouvoir étaient aussi transportés avec eux."UC'est comme ça que les mythes et légendes de chaque région furent mélangés."pLes anciennes ruines ont hérité des légendes des Ruines Alpha de Johto et des Colonnes Lances de Sinnoh."[C'est une preuve que les personnes de Johto et Sinnoh se sont bel et bien mélangées."J\PN! Je ne pensais pas te retrouver ici. C'est chouette de te revoir."<Mon nom est Cynthia. Je suis une Dresseuse de Pokémon."GLes Ruines Sinjoh me rappellent Sinnoh, la région d'où je viens."PAu début, je pensais que c'était parce qu'il neigeait beaucoup ici aussi."Mais ce n'était pas ça."HIl y a bien longtemps... Des gens de Sinnoh sont venus habiter ici."4Ils ont dû construire un temple par nostalgie.";C'est pour cela qu'on les appelle les Ruines Sinjoh..."Tu es..."Un Dresseur?"KCe Pokémon derrière toi... Je sens comme une présence familière..."MLe pouvoir de Dialga... de Palkia... Ou se peut-il que ce soit Giratina?"5Il est semblable, mais pas vraiment identique..."%Est-ce que ça serait... Arceus?".Peux-tu venir aux Ruines Sinjoh avec moi?"!Et amener Arceus avec toi...;["kA long time ago, people used to draw life from Pokémon and also give their lives to those Pokémon..."XThat shows that people and Pokémon used to be more closely bonded with each other."�When people moved from place to place, the myths and legends of Pokémon and their power would also be carried with those people."OThat's how myths and legends from each region are blended with each other."{The ancient ruins here have inherited the legends from both the Ruins of Alph in Johto and the Spear Pillar in Sinnoh."UThat is proof that the people from Johto and Sinnoh blended together as a group."I\PN! I did not expect to find you here. It is good to see you again."1My name is Cynthia. I am a Pokémon trainer."=The Sinjoh ruins remind me of Sinnoh, where I come from."EInitially, I thought it was because it snows a lot here as well."But that was not it."=A long time ago... people came from Sinnoh to live here.":They must have built a temple while longing for home."1That's why we call these the Sinjoh ruins..."You are..."A Pokémon trainer?"CThis Pokémon behind you... I can sense a familiar presence...">The power of Dialga... Palkia... Or could it be Giratina?",It's similar, but not quite the same..."Could it be.... Arceus?".Can you c