 south from this harbour."�However, this isn't a path that's normally taken without a boat. There are strong currents that make it very dangerous, so you'll have to be careful!"�Just continue due South from this harbor. When you see the water become bright blue, it means that Mt. Ember is nearby. You can't miss it!"<Continue due South from this harbor to reach Mt. Ember."eWhen you see the water become bright blue, it means that Mt. Ember is nearby. You can't miss it!"*Stop! Don't let them go to Mt. Ember!""Oh, no... I'm too late, am I?"�You see, Mt. Ember is a volcano located in the Sevii Islands, South from here. It's a protected area where we often go to make wildlife surveys."|It also happens to be the last known nesting area of a rare Pokémon called Moltres. I believe this is what they're after..."pIf Team Rocket goes and disturb Moltres... I don't want to think about what might happen if they do that..."?And without the Seagallop... How can anyone stop them now?"&Oh, you have Pokémon, don't you?"|In this case, there might still be hope! Follow me inside, I'll show you how you can get to Mt. Ember without the Seagallop."8tr going to mt. ember is bad because moltres blabla"HThey took it... I wasn't fast enough and they took the Seagallop..."(Oh my... What am I going to do now?"aThey said they were going to Mt. Ember... But without a boat, there's no way to follow them."Unless..."�You see, Mt. Ember is a volcano located in the Sevii Islands, \C[1]south from here\C[0]. It's a protected area where Cinnabar scientists often to make wildlife surveys."bUsually, I'd take the Seagallop to Knot Island to go there, but there might be another way..."JIf you surf from this harbour, you might be able to reach to volcano."�Just continue due South from this here. When you see the water become bright blue, it means that Mt. Ember is nearby. You can't miss it!"FContinue due \C[1]south from this harbor\C[0] to reach Mt. Ember.["hComme je l'ai dit plus tôt, la Mont Braise 